  "mawfish bones": {
    "general": `Mawfish Bones are acquired by cutting up Mawfish caught through Fishing. Go to Fisher Hai-Luk in Cetus, select the desired amount of Mawfish available, and select the "''Cut Fish''" option to extract the components. Each Mawfish cut yields one Mawfish Bones. Alternatively, Fisher Hai-Luk can sell Mawfish Bones in bundles of 20 among her rotating stock of "'''Daily Specials'''", which can be bought for Platinum.`,
    "blueprint": `Mawfish Bones are acquired by cutting up Mawfish caught through Fishing. Go to Fisher Hai-Luk in Cetus, select the desired amount of Mawfish available, and select the "''Cut Fish''" option to extract the components. Each Mawfish cut yields one Mawfish Bones. Alternatively, Fisher Hai-Luk can sell Mawfish Bones in bundles of 20 among her rotating stock of "'''Daily Specials'''", which can be bought for Platinum.`
  },
  "medjay predasite": {
    "general": "To obtain a Predasite as a companion, players must acquire one through Revivification with Son in the Necralisk, Deimos. This process requires capturing a Weakened Medjay Predasite during the '''Vome''' cycle via Conservation, after it has been attacked by the Infested. Additionally, players need a Mutagen and an Antigen, which can be purchased from Son using Entrati Standing, along with to initiate the Revivification process. A newly revived Predasite cannot be renamed, customized, Polarized, equipped with a Focus Lens, or earn Mastery Rank experience, but can equip an Orokin Reactor. In order to unlock these features, the player must Gild their Predasite by leveling it up to Rank 30 and then returning to Son along with 10 Son Token and 5,000 Standing.",
    "blueprint": "To obtain a Predasite as a companion, players must acquire one through Revivification with Son in the Necralisk, Deimos. This process requires capturing a Weakened Medjay Predasite during the '''Vome''' cycle via Conservation, after it has been attacked by the Infested. Additionally, players need a Mutagen and an Antigen, which can be purchased from Son using Entrati Standing, along with to initiate the Revivification process. A newly revived Predasite cannot be renamed, customized, Polarized, equipped with a Focus Lens, or earn Mastery Rank experience, but can equip an Orokin Reactor. In order to unlock these features, the player must Gild their Predasite by leveling it up to Rank 30 and then returning to Son along with 10 Son Token and 5,000 Standing."
  },
